1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:04,150
The world has fallen in love

2
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:07,820
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,110
I just want to understand you

4
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:15,490
Won't you open up to me?

5
00:00:22,410 --> 00:00:26,630
A fumbled exchange of words leaves a little taste of regret

6
00:00:28,090 --> 00:00:29,960
Enough to make me cry

7
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:35,300
I want to link my racing emotions to the beat of my heart

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,430
and put it all in tune

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,270
I lost sight of everything but my goal

10
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:51,940
and had something important fade away

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:58,200
Let's start all over

12
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:03,330
The world has fallen in love

13
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:06,580
An arrow of light shoots through my heart

14
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,170
I want to know everything about you

15
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:14,340
Won't you tell me more?

16
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:17,970
One inch feels like a million miles

17
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:20,890
as the days just seem to race by

18
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:25,310
I won't and can't ever forget

19
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,560
this brightest page of my life.

20
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,450
Get off!

21
00:01:53,170 --> 00:01:55,050
I accidentally fell in love...

22
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:57,680
...with the same person...

23
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:03,140
...as my best friend.

24
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:07,060
You'll feel better after drinking some water.

25
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:08,850
Thanks.

26
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,520
Wait, the money...

27
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:14,860
Oh, don't worry about that.

28
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:17,030
Thanks...

29
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:28,040
It's not like I'm feeling sick or anything,

30
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:29,920
but it's too late to tell him that.

31
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:32,880
Yoshioka.

32
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:36,380
Give me the water.

33
00:02:36,380 --> 00:02:37,340
Huh?!

34
00:02:37,340 --> 00:02:38,970
Don't give me that.

35
00:02:40,090 --> 00:02:41,260
I bought it,

36
00:02:43,100 --> 00:02:44,600
so I should get to drink it.

37
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:47,890
Wait, isn't this an...

38
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:48,850
In

39
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:48,850
...in-

40
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:50,980
-direct...

41
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:50,980
direct

42
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:53,230
...k-ki...

43
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:53,230
Ki

44
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:57,190
In-direct Ki...

45
00:02:58,950 --> 00:02:59,900
What?

46
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:03,120
No, uh...

47
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,620
Oh, are you a germaphobe or something?

48
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:10,960
No, that's not exactly it...

49
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:13,460
I didn't mean to stare like that.

50
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,040
Fine, I got it.

51
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:22,930
So cold! I'm chok—

52
00:03:22,930 --> 00:03:26,140
Are you okay? Let me grab a towel...

53
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:39,690
Sorry, looks like I kinda forgot it in the classroom.

54
00:03:39,690 --> 00:03:41,400
Just forget it.

55
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:43,240
I can't believe it...

56
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:48,240
The day where I finally feel embarrassed about my boorish facade has come.

57
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:55,790
But the reason everyone else dresses up and uses makeup

58
00:03:55,790 --> 00:03:58,000
is to look good for others, right?

59
00:03:58,670 --> 00:04:05,470
How is that different from me trying to look cute in front of the boys?

60
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:12,890
Those words are really ringing true right now.

61
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:14,730
Really loudly...

62
00:04:17,110 --> 00:04:18,730
Why am I acting all pure?!

63
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:18,900
pure

64
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:19,610
Insulting herself to keep her sanity

65
00:04:18,730 --> 00:04:21,280
I messed up my bag and made it dirty on purpose!

66
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,190
messed up

67
00:04:20,030 --> 00:04:20,740
dirty

68
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:20,900
Insulting herself to keep her sanity

69
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:22,450
Disgusting! I'm disgusting!

70
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:22,450
Insulting herself to keep her sanity

71
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:22,450
Disgusting!
I'm disgusting!

72
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,410
What's wrong?

73
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,870
Still feeling sick?

74
00:04:26,870 --> 00:04:29,160
No, I'm totally better now.

75
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:33,580
Really?

76
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:35,960
Really...

77
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:53,100
Huh?

78
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:57,980
You use perfume?

79
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,780
No, not at all.

80
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:04,950
Oh... must be your shampoo.

81
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:11,490
Well, what do you know. That turns me on.

82
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,550
Say something...

83
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:28,180
Come on, at least show some reaction.

84
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,220
Now I just look like a pervert.

85
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:36,520
Y-You should make it easier for me to tell you're joking.

86
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:41,440
How am I supposed to know what to say, silly...

87
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:46,490
I just got the cheapest shampoo they had at the supermarket.

88
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:52,030
Whether he was joking or not,
I should've gotten something better.

89
00:05:52,030 --> 00:05:55,620
It's such a hassle being in love.

90
00:05:55,620 --> 00:05:57,420
Oh, that reminds me.

91
00:05:57,420 --> 00:05:58,460
Of what?

92
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:02,250
I was supposed to pick up some
shampoo on the way home.

93
00:06:02,250 --> 00:06:04,800
You're welcome for the reminder, I guess.

94
00:06:06,550 --> 00:06:09,800
I need to go swing by the drug store.

95
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:13,430
Are you really sure you're better now?

96
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:15,270
Don't you worry!

97
00:06:15,270 --> 00:06:17,440
Alright then. Later.

98
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:26,360
I really do want to walk home with you, Kou,

99
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:30,990
but I wouldn't really feel right doing that.

100
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:34,700
Like I was betraying Yuuri.

101
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,290
Yuuri...

102
00:06:41,210 --> 00:06:42,630
I have to tell her.

103
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:46,130
I need to say I love Kou.

104
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:47,720
I have to tell her.

105
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:56,390
When you're in love, you become
aware of the smallest details.

106
00:06:56,390 --> 00:07:01,520
It's supposed to be a real hassle,
but the feelings that control you

107
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,940
also uplift your spirits.

108
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:05,900
Sorry for the delay.

109
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,860
Special Campaign!
Buy now and get a free
Ramune-chan Mascot!

110
00:07:06,440 --> 00:07:07,780
Do you have a point card?

111
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:08,860
Yes, right here.

112
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:10,070
Okay, I've scanned it in.

113
00:07:10,070 --> 00:07:11,320
Isn't that...

114
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,920
Payment of 3000 yen.

115
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:25,670
I need to tell Yuuri soon.

116
00:07:26,170 --> 00:07:28,050
Thank you very much.

117
00:07:32,970 --> 00:07:35,970
What will Yuuri think?

118
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:39,180
Will she start to hate me?

119
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:41,190
No, Yuuri wouldn't...

120
00:07:41,190 --> 00:07:42,140
Futaba?

121
00:07:50,190 --> 00:07:51,900
Yumi-chan?

122
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:57,540
Odds and evens! One, two, shoot!

123
00:07:57,540 --> 00:08:01,040
Naitou! What're you up to?

124
00:07:58,740 --> 00:08:00,540
Nice, I'm a cop.

125
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:07,130
Yumi-chan was my classmate in middle school.

126
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:10,670
We were very close friends.

127
00:08:11,130 --> 00:08:14,140
Splitting teams for cops and robbers.

128
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:16,010
Hey, let's play.

129
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:23,980
Yumi-chan had a crush on a boy named Naitou-kun,

130
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:25,350
I haven't played this since I was a kid!

131
00:08:25,690 --> 00:08:26,650
Same here.

132
00:08:26,650 --> 00:08:28,570
It's like we're back in elementary school!

133
00:08:28,570 --> 00:08:29,650
Isn't it?

134
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:32,150
Kou was standing behind them.

135
00:08:30,070 --> 00:08:31,530
Let me play too!

136
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:34,070
What, you serious?

137
00:08:34,070 --> 00:08:35,780
Let's all play together!

138
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,620
Really? Cops and robbers?

139
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:41,700
What, the girls are in too?

140
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:44,330
How about it, Futaba?

141
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:56,390
I guess... I'll play.

142
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:58,600
Then that's that!

143
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,720
I'm counting to one hundred!

144
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:05,810
One! Two! Three!

145
00:09:03,020 --> 00:09:06,190
Everything was peaceful throughout my first year in middle school.

146
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:15,070
But when the next year rolled around...

147
00:09:15,070 --> 00:09:17,490
Hey, isn't Yoshioka kinda cute?

148
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:19,700
Yeah, she totally is.

149
00:09:19,700 --> 00:09:21,290
She's so refined.

150
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:24,540
The other girls could learn a thing or two from her.

151
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:31,630
I started drawing attention, for better or worse.

152
00:09:32,130 --> 00:09:35,380
Futaba's just putting on an act for the guys.

153
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:37,590
Right? She pisses me off.

154
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:39,600
Futaba.

155
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,350
But even then...

156
00:09:41,350 --> 00:09:46,190
They're just jealous that the boys are all over you.

157
00:09:46,980 --> 00:09:49,520
You know it's not your fault.

158
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,560
Idiots, all of them.

159
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:56,280
She was the only one who stuck by my side.

160
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:58,910
I'll always be there for you.

161
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:02,080
But one day...

162
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:05,700
...Yumi-chan suddenly stopped talking to me.

163
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:07,920
Wait up, I'll go too!

164
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:11,170
Yumi, are you sure you wanna leave Futaba behind?

165
00:10:11,170 --> 00:10:13,800
Um... yeah, don't worry about it.

166
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:20,890
My last remaining ally left my side
without ever telling me why.

167
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:27,060
I don't think I've seen you since graduation.

168
00:10:28,230 --> 00:10:29,230
Yeah...

169
00:10:34,940 --> 00:10:36,990
Remember Naitou?

170
00:10:38,610 --> 00:10:40,820
The guy you had a crush on?

171
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:49,080
Man, I remember asking you for advice about him all the time.

172
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:53,630
Yeah...

173
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:55,460
Good times...

174
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:59,680
What a lie. I'd erase that from my memory if I could.

175
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:03,510
I just don't know what else to say

176
00:11:03,510 --> 00:11:08,020
to someone who deserted me without any explanation.

177
00:11:08,020 --> 00:11:09,480
Hey, actually...

178
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:14,940
I've always wanted to apologize to you.

179
00:11:17,570 --> 00:11:18,780
You see, one day,

180
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:23,870
a girl told me that you also liked Naitou-kun.

181
00:11:26,910 --> 00:11:30,370
When I went to ask you about it...

182
00:11:32,370 --> 00:11:33,540
Futaba!

183
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:40,260
I saw your eyes on him.

184
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:47,680
I thought, "I'm the one who loved him first!"

185
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:53,940
I know that liking someone first doesn't actually mean anything.

186
00:11:55,520 --> 00:11:58,570
But by then, I'd lost my reasoning

187
00:11:58,570 --> 00:12:01,400
and was boiling with rage at you.

188
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:12,540
I knew that if I left, you'd be all alone. Sorry—

189
00:12:12,540 --> 00:12:14,170
Yumi-chan, I...

190
00:12:15,630 --> 00:12:19,420
I never felt that way about Naitou-kun.

191
00:12:21,630 --> 00:12:25,840
Looking back, there was even another boy I liked.

192
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:32,140
I knew that Naitou-kun was friends with Kou, so I wanted to ask if he'd heard anything,

193
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:36,310
or if he knew anything about how Kou was.

194
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:43,150
Yumi-chan got the wrong idea.

195
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:44,910
Futaba...

196
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,120
Sorry.

197
00:12:50,410 --> 00:12:52,870
When you fall in love with the person your friend likes,

198
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:58,130
this is what happens.

199
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:05,050
Sorry, I've gotta go.

200
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:09,010
I'm happy I got to see you again.

201
00:13:16,270 --> 00:13:18,610
I was naive.

202
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:28,490
I was hoping that Yuuri might not get mad at me when I told her...

203
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:36,920
But just like Yumi-chan, she'll probably end up falling prey to her feelings

204
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,710
and be overcome with hate.

205
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:45,090
Why did she have to show up now of all times?

206
00:13:46,010 --> 00:13:49,470
It feels like God is testing me.

207
00:13:50,430 --> 00:13:55,140
But... I can't lie about my feelings for Kou anymore.

208
00:13:57,100 --> 00:14:00,440
I really have no choice but to tell her!

209
00:14:02,190 --> 00:14:03,280
I have to...

210
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:11,740
How many days has it been since I said that?

211
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:13,950
Just talk to her already, dammit!

212
00:14:13,950 --> 00:14:16,330
Useless! Useless! Useless!

213
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:17,710
Good morning.

214
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,880
Futaba-chan, good morning.

215
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,290
Morning...

216
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:29,050
Makita.

217
00:14:30,090 --> 00:14:32,890
I brought the CD you texted me about yesterday.

218
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:35,930
Thank you!

219
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:40,650
They text each other?

220
00:14:40,650 --> 00:14:43,270
There's a secret cover he did of his own song on it.

221
00:14:43,270 --> 00:14:44,270
Yeah, yeah!

222
00:14:44,270 --> 00:14:45,690
You gotta listen to it.

223
00:14:48,450 --> 00:14:50,490
Yuuri's so lucky.

224
00:14:48,450 --> 00:14:51,030
What song's your favorite?

225
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:55,370
It's all so easy when you've got that cute personality established.

226
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:55,370
If I had to pick, it'd be this one.

227
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:59,830
What was that? My jealousy's taking over!

228
00:14:59,830 --> 00:15:02,040
This is the one used in that commercial.

229
00:15:04,710 --> 00:15:05,750
But...

230
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:13,470
I also understand why Yuuri wants people to think she's cute.

231
00:15:13,470 --> 00:15:16,060
What is this emotion?

232
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:17,430
Futaba-chan.

233
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:20,640
Mabichi-kun lent me a CD!

234
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:22,860
That's great...

235
00:15:24,570 --> 00:15:26,110
Murao-san, good morning.

236
00:15:26,110 --> 00:15:27,900
Morning.

237
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:28,990
Hey.

238
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:34,870
Yuuri is just

239
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:38,540
doing everything she can.

240
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:42,330
She's nothing like me, holding everything in.

241
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:44,250
I'm the worst.

242
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:51,760
Yoshioka.

243
00:15:54,890 --> 00:15:56,850
What?! What is it?

244
00:15:57,350 --> 00:15:58,810
You don't know?

245
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,770
Tell me!

246
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:09,740
Your part of the report had way too many things wrong with it.

247
00:16:06,190 --> 00:16:12,150
Class 2-2
Yoshioka Futaba

248
00:16:06,190 --> 00:16:12,150
Leadership Course Report

249
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:12,150
They said we had to redo it and hand it in again.

250
00:16:14,530 --> 00:16:17,120
You got it...

251
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,490
Class 2-2
Yoshioka Futaba

252
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,490
Leadership Course Report

253
00:16:19,450 --> 00:16:21,500
You feeling alright?

254
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:35,840
I'll tell her! I swear I'll tell her...

255
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:36,890
I'll say it!

256
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:41,980
I can't say it...

257
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:45,980
Futaba-chan, not feeling hungry? Are you sick?

258
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:48,820
I bought too much out of habit.

259
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,360
Yuuri, want a chocolate roll?

260
00:16:53,650 --> 00:16:56,570
What about anpan? Or a yakisoba roll?

261
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:59,160
I-I couldn't eat that much.

262
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:02,620
Yeah, right.

263
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:05,830
Murao-san, want any?

264
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:07,580
Not really.

265
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:09,340
Figures.

266
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,300
Maybe I should return them.

267
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:13,970
I don't think they let you return bread.

268
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:16,720
I'll go and check anyway.

269
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:18,220
Futaba-chan!

270
00:17:18,930 --> 00:17:19,560
Yeah?

271
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,100
Want me to come with you?

272
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:23,390
I'll be fine by myself.

273
00:17:29,230 --> 00:17:30,820
Did I...

274
00:17:31,110 --> 00:17:35,320
...do something bad to Futaba-chan?

275
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,780
I'm going to go after her.

276
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:52,420
Excuse me, so you know the girl who always buys a lot...

277
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:53,760
I want to stay friends with Yuuri.

278
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:58,590
I also want to stay in love with Kou.

279
00:17:59,090 --> 00:18:04,560
Guess it's impossible to eat my cake and have it too.

280
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:09,270
Kou probably doesn't even see me as a girl anyway.

281
00:18:09,270 --> 00:18:12,400
In that case I can keep it a secret from Yuuri

282
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:15,860
and just watch him from afar.

283
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:21,120
Kou, what are you doing?!
I almost had a heart—

284
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:25,620
Shut up.

285
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:27,330
Close! Close! Close! Close!

286
00:18:33,550 --> 00:18:34,840
Kou!

287
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,260
Crap, he's here.

288
00:18:36,260 --> 00:18:38,050
Tanaka-sensei?

289
00:18:38,050 --> 00:18:39,550
Where'd you go?

290
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,970
Kou!

291
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:48,730
Why are you hiding from him?

292
00:18:50,310 --> 00:18:54,610
He's so stubborn about having dinner together.

293
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:58,900
Why not just do it?

294
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:09,870
His silence is telling me not to pry any further.

295
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:15,840
Did you change your shampoo?

296
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:22,800
I wanted to turn you on.

297
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:32,190
Oh, you were right.

298
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:37,530
It does get awkward when you can't tell if it's a joke.

299
00:19:39,490 --> 00:19:43,030
Right, well my brother's gone, so I'll be off.

300
00:19:44,990 --> 00:19:47,740
Watch from afar?

301
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:51,330
I try my hardest to make something happen given the slightest chance.

302
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:55,840
I even changed my shampoo for him.

303
00:19:55,840 --> 00:19:59,260
I'm doing all sorts of sneaky things behind Yuuri's back.

304
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,010
Oh, right.

305
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:05,600
Makita was looking for you.

306
00:20:06,970 --> 00:20:10,980
She seemed really worried.
Did something happen?

307
00:20:13,850 --> 00:20:17,400
Yuuri was worried about me?

308
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:21,360
You see?

309
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:25,070
That's the kind of girl she is.

310
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:29,870
I knew Yuuri was a good girl.

311
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:37,250
She's an incredibly dear friend of mine.

312
00:20:37,250 --> 00:20:40,300
When you talked to me that day,

313
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:43,130
can you imagine just how happy I was?

314
00:20:44,050 --> 00:20:48,640
That's why I'll never leave you alone.

315
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:50,220
I promise.

316
00:20:54,730 --> 00:20:57,310
That's why I want us to stay friends.

317
00:21:01,150 --> 00:21:06,700
But because she's so dear to me, I have to tell her.

318
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:09,370
Whatever happens after that..

319
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:12,330
...is up to Yuuri.

320
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:28,970
Futaba-chan!

321
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:34,640
The donut shop in front of the station is having a 100-yen sale.

322
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:37,730
Wanna stop by with me?

323
00:21:38,770 --> 00:21:39,770
Yuuri...

324
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,110
Sure.

325
00:21:46,110 --> 00:21:49,700
Today, I might lose...

326
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:54,040
...a very dear friend.

327
00:22:00,630 --> 00:22:05,760
In a town beset by a sudden shower,

328
00:22:05,760 --> 00:22:11,140
I say "See you later", and wave goodbye.

329
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:16,600
As I watch you pass through the ticket gate, I think:

330
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:21,900
"It never goes according to plan, does it?"

331
00:22:21,900 --> 00:22:31,620
Everything seemed incredibly fragile that day,

332
00:22:31,620 --> 00:22:37,210
but it passed, as days tend to do.

333
00:22:38,370 --> 00:22:47,760
The rails carry you away

334
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:56,020
leaving me alone on our usual path.

335
00:22:57,140 --> 00:23:06,650
The words I prepared for you are so simple,

336
00:23:06,650 --> 00:23:15,370
so why can't I say them?

337
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:22,330
Why can't I?

338
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:39,890
NEXT TIME...

339
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:29,340
Even if one of you succeeds,

340
00:23:29,340 --> 00:23:33,090
I'll still be on both of your sides.

341
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:36,810
Good luck, you two.
